            </div>


            <!-- =========================
                 SUMMARY
            ========================== -->

            <div class="alert alert-info mt-4 mb-0"
                 style="background-color:#cfe2ff; border:0; color:#123c73;">

                <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-0 mb-3"
                    style="color:#123c73;">

                    Summary :

                </h2>

                <p class="mb-0"
                   style="color:#123c73;">

                    Parameters receive input in the function definition, while arguments are the actual values passed during a function call. In Python, flexible and reusable functions can be created using positional arguments, keyword arguments, default parameters, <strong>*args</strong>, and <strong>**kwargs</strong>.

                </p>

            </div>


